 yeah I don't  really believe and I'm not you're right  I'm not a conspiracy theorist in the  sense that usually conspiracy theories  revolve around supreme intelligence that  is somehow masterminding and I don't  have that much confidence in people's  intelligence to get that right so that's  where the conspiracy theories when we  usually fall down but I am interested in  abuses of power and part of power and  abusing power usually has to do with  secrecy and so you have to pierce that  veil of secrecy or try to in order to be  able to get at and to understand those  abuses are you optimistic that this will  get worked out or are you pessimistic in  the short term I'm pessimistic but  hopeful as Richard Clarke says in the  film everybody said we couldn't do  agreements relating to nuclear weapons  we did it was everyone said the same  thing about chemical weapons we did I  think we can get it right with cyber  weapons but we have to have the will to  do it and right now the norm as a former  NSA jag also says in the film is that  there should be no norm that there are  no rules and that's not a very good norm  that puts us all at risk  you
 

